  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Prolintane is a stimulant drug classified among other psychostimulants and nootropics, a group used for conditions such as attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. It is considered experimental and does not appear to be an approved medicine today, so its current availability is unclear.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1653730&quot;>Wikidata Q1653730</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>prolintane</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N06BX14</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13438&quot;>DB13438</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/14592&quot;>14592</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:134898&quot;>134898</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1653730&quot;>Q1653730</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C15H23N</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>217.356 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
